atlas surface
# The surface compiler and the learning organ above it. SurfaceIR consumes every
# app grammar + addressing + authority + evidence and compiles what an actor sees
# and can do; it renders affordances, it never authorizes. Its action traces feed
# SurfaceMotifLearning, which proposes better presentation/adjacency to the
# AddressPlane -- closing the learning loop (riff SS10) without ever mutating
# semantic truth. That organ was called Aurekai until the bare name was returned
# to the institution it names; the id changed and nothing referenced it, which is
# itself the reason the collision went unnoticed for so long.

architecture surface-ir
  canonical_name SurfaceIR
  family surface
  domain Surface / Compilation
  layer surface
  semantic_question What should this actor see and be able to do, compiled from all relevant state?
  purpose The surface compiler. Consumes the nine app grammars plus addressing, authority and evidence, and emits a rendered surface and an action trace. It renders affordances; the exact Authority check still runs at effect time.
  maturity implemented
  owns SurfaceIR
  consumes DocType
  consumes SurfaceGrammar
  consumes DealState
  consumes TicketState
  consumes DerivedView
  consumes KnowledgeClaim
  consumes ShareGrant
  consumes RepresentationHistory
  consumes OpportunityEligibility
  consumes FortificationPlan
  consumes RouteAdvertisement
  consumes Authority
  publishes ActionTrace
  publishes SurfaceDelta
  invariant SurfaceRuntime keeps Actual (the exact derived Scene revision), Possible (declared lenses and apertures), Presence (actor scope plus transient interaction posture) and Material (declared owner-query plan) as separate planes; none is an identity, authority, availability, proof, commitment or effect claim
  invariant a SurfaceDelta applies only from its exact prior Scene digest; a changed digest carries a complete successor Scene, while an offline or mismatched client asks its owner-side carrier to reconcile and never applies a queued or partial owner result
  internal_calculus subject-first aperture: HTMX requests native, host-checked HTML fragments. Browser forms use the same typed Studio owner contracts as JSON carriers, and the server compiles owner receipts into readable result grammar. Content Home reads the canonical CMS tables for usable page/learning/application work rather than exposing schemas as the human entry point; a selected public URL remains only proposed route context until the authenticated ForeignTwin observe effect runs.
  invariant a landing-page public-address handoff is only user-proposed route context; the native ForeignTwin observer still requires an explicit signed-in observe effect
  invariant a human Studio request receives a server-rendered result fragment rather than a raw JSON receipt; machine carriers retain their explicit JSON contract
  invariant a human CMS write submits ordinary form fields through the native content type, while the CMS alone compiles and validates its typed stored representation
  forbidden_inference a surface renders an action -> the action is authorized (Authority gates at effect time; the surface only shows affordances)
  forbidden_inference a fact is off-surface -> the fact does not exist (a surface is a projection, not the fabric)
  forbidden_inference a pasted public address -> fetched evidence, a ForeignTwin, canonical truth, or authority over the foreign system
  forbidden_inference a rendered CMS save result -> publication, public readability, or authority outside the selected content lifecycle
  source_lineage frontend fold -- surfaces as projections over shared semantic objects
