  witness cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/tests/surface_pattern_test.sh proves one CMS-authored descriptor serves a person and a machine the same records in the same order, that a declared authority is refused in both projections, and that an undeclared pattern is not invented
  invariant a surface pattern is a CMS descriptor naming what it reads, its effect class and the authority it requires; the organ holds the render primitives, so a content write can add a surface but never introduce markup
  invariant a pattern's human and machine projections are compiled from one descriptor and one query; the same records in the same order reach HTMX and JSON, because there is one implementation rather than two carriers of one capability
  invariant the carrier symmetry holds at the error boundary too: an unauthenticated machine receives the refusal in its own grammar, because an auth gate that hands machines an HTML page breaks the same-capability claim exactly where every unauthenticated caller meets it
  invariant a declared API surface answers for its own errors and is never routed onward as an unbound address; a 404 fallthrough is right for a bare semantic path and wrong for an organ that already said something precise
  invariant a territory projection selects fields from one shared content type rather than owning a copy of the subjects; four territories reading one type with four field sets is the projection claim, and four types with similar rows would be its refutation
  invariant every page a person opens reads the authored navigation, whether the organ renders it server-side or the page swaps it in; a nav fragment that serves correctly while every landing page shows compiled links is a fragment nobody renders
  invariant a page that declares a swap loads the runtime that performs it; an hx-get with no htmx is inert decoration that renders the fallback forever and looks correct in the source
  forbidden_inference a fragment endpoint answering -> the pages that should use it rendering it
  invariant a landing surface is authored state, not a file under a site root; a file is a fine way to serve a page and a poor way to own one, and thirteen files each carrying their own navigation is what made a single nav change a thirteen-file edit
  invariant an authored page is served before the static file for the same route, so migration proceeds page by page and an unauthored route keeps working
  invariant a page declares its own title; an organ appending the institution name produced the institution named twice on the front page
  invariant an authored surface never displaces an existing machine contract: a territory root answers machines with its discovery descriptor, and adding a second machine view of one route is the drift this estate spends its effort preventing
  invariant a surface is not classified as a page or an application; it composes three layers over one addressed closure -- authored state, live closure lenses, and action apertures -- and the difference between a narrative page and an operating workspace is the balance among them, not a change of architecture
  invariant the authored layer holds copy and arrangement, the closure layer names patterns that render live addressed state, and the action layer names the subject whose admitted operations the surface offers; none of the three owns what another owns
  invariant the action layer is fetched rather than baked, because what a person may do depends on who they are and a page rendered for everyone cannot say; an anonymous reader is told operations exist and are not offered rather than shown a menu that lies
  forbidden_inference a declared lens or aperture -> a working or permitted one (a lens names a pattern that still enforces its own authority, and an aperture is offered only where the grammar applies and the actor is admitted)
  invariant a surface renders at a requested extent -- chip, card, section, page or workspace -- and the extent changes how much of one closure is shown, never which subject is addressed; a workspace appearing elsewhere as a card is a projection rather than a second implementation
  invariant chip, card and section are fragments with no document chrome, because a surface embedded in another surface must not bring its own document
  invariant only a workspace carries the action layer; a page shows authored state and its closure without implying that anything may be done from it
  forbidden_inference a smaller extent -> a lesser subject (the same closure is addressed at every extent)
  invariant an operation owned elsewhere posts to its owner; the aperture renders the form and the native organ performs the act, so no credential passes through the surface that drew it
  invariant a surface with one obvious action leads with that operation's form rather than a link to it; a list of one is a menu pretending to be a choice
  invariant a contract names the words on its own button and the type of its own fields; deriving them put the identifier open on a sign-in form and would have rendered a password as readable text
  invariant a native form works without a script runtime, so the owner accepts what a form posts; requiring JSON at that edge would make signing in depend on JavaScript
  invariant the action layer is carried at page and workspace and omitted below; a chip, card or section is a reference to a surface and there is no room to act inside a reference
  invariant authoring a route never removes a machine contract that route already had; the page declares machine_view deferred where a native owner answers machines, so the rule is a field rather than a route literal in the organ
  invariant an authored pane is rendered only to a caller who can fill it; htmx declares [45].. swap:false, so a fragment answering 401 leaves its placeholder on screen permanently and the page reports loading forever
  invariant a surface that withholds a pane for want of a session offers the operation that would grant one; withholding without offering is a dead end wearing the clothes of a loading state
  forbidden_inference a green surface test -> a working surface (the extent asked for decides what is rendered, and a test that asks for the extent that works proves only that one)
  invariant a surface pattern reads a CMS type or a native organ, and the catalogue names which; a pattern that read an organ advertised itself as reading nothing while it worked
  invariant an organ a descriptor names is a bare bonfyre- identifier resolved inside the estate's own bin directory, never a path; content declares which organ is asked and can never choose what executes
  invariant a registry row whose fields are the descriptor's own field names is the header; testing for a literal column label was true of one organ's output and of nothing else
  invariant a panel carries its own title and caption, so every page composing it as a lens gets the same label and none of them can disagree about what the panel is
  invariant an organ that will not answer renders as a stated gap, never as an empty list; an empty panel reads as nothing to see, which is a different claim
  known_gap cms and studio remain applications rather than authored pages, which is what they are; habitat, property, market, sources and agents were files and are now composed from descriptors
  invariant an authored surface keeps its compiled route as a floor beneath it; the authored page declines when the CMS cannot be read, and without that floor a store outage turns a carrier surface into a 404 rather than into an older page
  invariant a client that sent a wildcard Accept is not a machine; representation follows what a client asked for, and treating the absence of an ask for HTML as an ask for JSON silently changes what every plain shell fetch has been reading
  forbidden_inference a handler that never answers in production -> dead code (the a2a suite runs this organ with no CMS at all, which is the only condition under which the compiled floor answers, and the only reason the deletion was caught)
  invariant a static asset carries an ETag that is its own content digest and answers a conditional request with 304 and no body; no-cache without a validator is not caching, it is re-downloading with extra steps
  invariant an asset is reusable while it refreshes, so a deploy costs one stale view rather than a choice between speed and correctness
  measured a warm page view fell from 923ms and ~29KB over the wire to 314ms and 4.6KB once the assets carried validators; the server itself was never slow, answering in ~165ms of which ~155ms is round trip
  forbidden_inference a fast server -> a fast page (every panel on an authored surface arrives as a later fragment, so the page is as slow as the runtime those fragments wait on)
  invariant every authored page carries the institution's machine constellation in its head, so a reader who arrived at a page can reach the same institution's agent card, MCP descriptor, crate, field and federated identity; expecting foreign systems to be discoverable while publishing our own only where it happened to be emitted is a standard applied in one direction
  invariant speculation candidates come from the authored navigation, which is what this institution addresses, and never from a foreign origin or a relative href; a prefetch is a request made on the visitor's behalf and it must not be made to someone else's server
  invariant speculation eagerness is moderate, firing on intent rather than at load; prefetching the whole navigation on every page view spends a visitor's bandwidth to improve our own numbers
  invariant a below-fold panel declares content-visibility with an intrinsic size, so an expressive page stays cheap without a JavaScript virtualization layer and the scrollbar does not move under the reader
  forbidden_inference a linked machine representation -> an authorized one (the manifest says where a representation is, never who may act on it)
  forbidden_inference a speculated path -> a visited one
  known_gap account, cms, studio and habitat are still files; login and signup showed the shape -- authored copy, a declared operation, a form posting to its owner -- and the remaining four differ only in how much closure and action they carry
  witness /property answers at five extents from 43 bytes to 2841, fragments carry no document, and the subject's heading is identical at every one
  known_gap login, signup, account, cms and studio are still files. That is a migration backlog, not a boundary: an earlier note here claimed they were applications rather than authored pages, which was true of site_page and false of the CMS -- their authored copy, their closure lenses and their action apertures each have an owner already, and only the composition is unbuilt
  witness /property renders all three layers on one route: authored hero and doors, a closure lens, and an action list that offers an admitted operator Property.investigateOwnership and tells an anonymous reader two operations exist and are not offered
  known_gap the Observatory replaces the shared nav with its own institution-specific links by design; that one nav stays compiled and is the single deliberate exception
  invariant a pattern's declared authority distinguishes a session scope from an institutional grant: a bare word is a scope, and <institution>:<role> is a grant inside that estate, because a persona holding institutional write is not the same claim as a write-scoped session
  invariant a subject whose kind is a container for many things resolves its apertures against its classified kind; ForeignTwin covers a tax roll and a specification, and offering both the same operations would make the aperture list a statement about storage rather than about the thing
  invariant a role requirement is satisfied by a higher role and refused by a lower one in the same institution; a surface that admits every authenticated member of an estate is checking membership, not role
  witness cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/tests/nightgrid_lattice_test.sh signs in eight declared personas and proves a read-role member is refused a write-role projection its admin-role peer reads
  invariant a descriptor that fails identifier validation renders nothing and says so; an unsafe pattern is refused rather than sanitized into an approximate surface
  invariant a public surface serves published rows only; status_filter defaults to published and a pattern that reads a type where status is not meaningful must declare 'any' explicitly, which the catalogue then shows
  invariant a pattern declares the row-level visibility flags its read type carries, so a type marking rows unpublished or guest-forbidden has those rows excluded by the surface rather than by the reader
  invariant the estate publishes its own read surfaces at /_surface/ with each pattern's read type, effect class and authority requirement; a machine discovers what is served rather than guessing pattern names
  forbidden_inference a pattern listed in the catalogue -> a pattern this caller may read (the catalogue reports the requirement; the pattern still enforces it)
  forbidden_inference an entry existing in an authored type -> that entry being publicly served (publication state and row visibility both gate before a surface renders it)
  forbidden_inference a pattern descriptor exists -> the pattern is served (a descriptor naming a type the store does not carry yields an empty fragment and the page keeps its compiled fallback)
  forbidden_inference a compiled fallback rendering -> the authored content agreeing with it (a fallback is a resilience path, never cached truth)
  known_gap the pattern compiler compiles list-shaped read patterns over authored CMS types into both projections, with publication state, row visibility, declared authority and a self-describing catalogue; arbitrary subject/view compilation across the full app-grammar estate is still owed, and effectful patterns (Join, Checkout, Approve) still have bespoke handlers because a descriptor must not be able to declare an effect
invariant the authored Production studio mounts supported research, product, process and schema controllers against existing native workspace record identities; composition does not implement an arbitrary skill or grant any external operation
  invariant public reusable designs contain only the reviewed title, purpose, panel arrangement and supported handoffs; private source bodies, findings, database bytes, people, credentials and original saved-record identities are excluded
  invariant an interrupted design publication retains its exact payload and baseline until native page readback confirms committed, unchanged or conflicting state; a user must explicitly retry an unchanged baseline and changed publication is never overwritten by recovery
  source_path cmd/BonfyreSurfaceScene/runtime/authored-workspace-view.mjs
  source_path cmd/BonfyreSurfaceScene/runtime/authored-publication.mjs
  source_path scripts/materialize_authored_workspace.mjs
  source_path integrations/browser/publication-research.mjs
  witness scripts/tests/authored-publication-browser.test.mjs exercises the actual native production editor, lost post-commit acknowledgement, anonymous design inspection, independent reuse in another account, withdrawal and unreadable-outcome recovery without duplicate writes
  witness cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/tests/publication_research_browser.mjs carries exact retained text and receipts into native research, captures a selected quotation, prepares a product opportunity, saves both working records and reopens them; concurrent changes and source duplicates are explicitly tested
  forbidden_inference four implemented instrument controllers or a composed publication -> completion of the 388 donor workflows, working foreign providers or permission to publish private material
  interacts installed-production-publishes-reviewed-design

architecture object-grammar
  canonical_name ObjectGrammar
  owns ObjectContract
  owns ActionAperture
  owns AtomicForm
  consumes Authority
  consumes AddressExpr
  consumes SubjectClosure
  publishes SurfaceGrammar
  publishes SemanticOperation
  family surface
  domain Surface / Institutional grammar
  layer surface
  semantic_question What kinds of thing may exist here, how does one enter the world, and what must a person actually be asked?
  purpose Separates three questions that are routinely confused: what may exist (ObjectContract), how something enters the world (an action aperture), and how an existing thing is addressed (AddressPlane). The middle question has no home unless apertures are computed, because the thing being created cannot yet be addressed -- so an aperture is resolved from the parent closure, and the operation exists before any instance does.
  maturity implemented
  node_types ObjectContract
  node_types ActionAperture
  node_types AtomicForm
  edge_types applies_to
  edge_types admits_operation
  invariant an aperture is offered only when the grammar applies to this subject kind and the actor's authority satisfies the contract; an operation the actor cannot perform is omitted rather than shown disabled, because an aperture list is a statement about this actor rather than a menu with locked entries
  invariant a compiled native SurfaceProgram may lower subject_apertures only from its published World's exact declared subject: it selects only published ObjectContracts whose declared applicability exactly matches that subject kind, filters every link through the current authority closure, and hands the operation to the existing AtomicForm/native owner rather than inventing a surface-local effect
  invariant the operation exists before the instance does; Event.declare is resolved on an institution while no Event exists, so nothing has to address an imaginary subject
  invariant an AtomicForm renders only the unresolved human variables of a semantic operation; every fact the closure can lawfully answer is shown as resolved context and never re-asked
  invariant resolved context stays visible rather than hidden, so a person can audit that the system decided the organizer is them
  invariant birth mode is declared and distinguishes what actually happens: DECLARE allocates a subject, ATTACH binds an existing one, PROPOSE creates institutional demand without effect, INVOKE performs an operation owned elsewhere, DERIVE creates nothing
  invariant a subject kind that does not fit the grammar's bound is refused rather than truncated; a silently shortened kind would match a different contract's applicability
  forbidden_inference an offered aperture -> a completed effect (the grammar applies and the actor is admitted; the native owner still owns what happens)
  forbidden_inference a SurfaceProgram aperture link -> a completed effect, a durable grant, a valid future submission, or an operation not declared by the resolved ObjectContract
  forbidden_inference a rendered AtomicForm -> an admitted submission (the operation is still gated at submit by Authority, by the contract's birth policy, and by the owner of the effect)
  forbidden_inference an INVOKE or DERIVE aperture -> a record to create (settlement is owned by Finance and MoneyGraph, and an economics result is computed on address rather than stored)
  invariant a DERIVE computes and returns; declining to store is only half of it, and an operation that neither writes nor computes is a refusal wearing an operation's name while its aperture advertises something the estate cannot do
  invariant a derivation is produced from the owner of its inputs every time it is addressed, which is why it is never written down: a stored derivation outlives its inputs and a computed one cannot
  invariant a derivation addressed at a subject with no corpus says so rather than returning an empty result that reads like an answer
  forbidden_inference a derived result -> a fact about the world (it summarises what this institution observed and inherits every limit of those observations)
  witness Property.economics over three real parcel sources returns 499,388, 109,576 and 726,756 observations computed live from the columnar estate, with stored=false
  source_path cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/src/main.c
  source_path schemas/control/foundry-behavior-specs.json
  source_path cmd/BonfyreCMS/tools/compile_foundry_behavior.mjs
  witness cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/tests/foundry_behavior_owner_test.sh
  witness cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/tests/aperture_test.sh proves all five birth modes behave differently -- DECLARE and PROPOSE allocate identity, ATTACH binds an existing ForeignTwin subject with the Matrix subject count unchanged across the call, DERIVE and INVOKE create nothing -- and that a second object grammar was wired by authoring alone -- BudgetRequest births in PROPOSE mode with its own identity prefix and route from its declared lens, on the same binary that births Events -- and that a DERIVE submission creates nothing, an INVOKE is refused as owned elsewhere, a DECLARE allocates a Matrix subject whose id the authored CMS body carries, and that the same subject yields three different aperture sets to an anonymous caller, a read-role member and an admin persona, and that Event.declare asks five human fields while five more are closed by the institution's own closure
  witness cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/tests/surface_pattern_contract_test.sh proves a CUE-compiled subject_apertures SurfaceProgram slot resolves a published World's institution subject, renders its applicable published ObjectContract action, and reaches the native /_aperture/form backed by /_aperture/submit
  invariant a birth allocates identity before it writes the body: the Matrix binds the subject first, so an authored body never describes a subject that does not exist, and a failed allocation leaves no orphaned row
  invariant when identity is allocated and the body write then fails, the caller is told exactly that rather than receiving an error that looks like nothing happened; a retry has to know a subject already exists
  invariant authority is re-checked at submit and not only at render; a form rendered an hour ago is not a grant, and a revocation between the two is honoured
  invariant birth mode decides what may happen before anything is created: a DERIVE submission creates nothing because a stored derivation outlives its inputs, and an INVOKE writes no record here because the effect and its state are owned by another organ
  forbidden_inference a completed birth -> a published, occurred, or onward-authorized thing (it exists in its declared initial state and nothing more)
  invariant birth binds three things or the subject is unreachable: the subject itself, a readable address, and a presence. Resolution joins address to presence, so an address bound without one is a row nobody reads
  invariant the address is a resolution route and never the identity: the slug follows a title a person may change, and the subject id is a digest that does not. A slug collision is disambiguated by the identity rather than by refusing the birth, because two things may honestly share a title
  invariant a presence inherits its world from the institution rather than defaulting; a demo institution projecting into LIVE would place synthetic state in the real world
  invariant the organ holds no knowledge of any particular object: body type, human fields, identity prefix and route segment all come from the contract, so wiring a new grammar is an authoring act and never a code change
  invariant a behavior family is expanded before publication into exact ObjectContracts; runtime lookup remains exact applies_to_kind equality and an unresolved owner/address closure emits no contract
  invariant the authored body is assembled from the fields the contract says a person supplies; naming one object's fields in the birth handler would make it the second place that knows what that object is
  invariant a required field is required because a contract asks for it, not because the handler names it; a grammar that asks for no title is not forced to have one
  invariant which field names a thing is the contract's answer, not a default; every object defaulting to a title gave every budget request the same route
  invariant a birth writes its own receipt as a never-overwritten record, in the shape foreign observations already use; the receipt id is the evidence_ref the subject, the address and the presence were bound under, so the file is what those three already point at rather than a new claim
  invariant a birth whose receipt cannot be written still succeeded and says so; the institutional state exists, and reporting failure would deny a thing that is real
  invariant a birth binds the edge to the closure it was declared in; an institution known only as a string inside an authored body is readable but not traversable, and invisible to anything asking what an institution contains
  invariant a birth emits its write set as a FactDelta at the moment of the transaction, because that is the only moment it is knowable; reconstructing it afterwards from three separate stores is the archaeology a delta exists to prevent
  invariant a surface that carries time declares which field holds it and which direction matters; comparison is lexical on ISO-8601 so a malformed value fails to match rather than being silently treated as now
  invariant an emitted delta is consumed and recomputes only the derivations its write set named; rebuilding every index on every birth is the whole-answer recomputation a delta exists to avoid
  invariant an applied delta is acknowledged by a separate immutable receipt bound to its exact filename and bytes, never by overwriting or deleting the producer event; the captured input remains journaled so a newly published version cannot erase failed pending work
  forbidden_inference an applied delta -> a correct index (it records that the recomputation ran over what the write set named)
  invariant ATTACH binds a subject that already exists and refuses to create one; an attachment that silently declares its own target is a declaration wearing another name, and the caller could not tell the difference
  invariant a claim is recorded as an edge rather than an object, so claiming something a ForeignTwin already represents cannot produce a rival record the institution would later have to choose between
  forbidden_inference a recorded claim -> a verified one (it is an assertion; AssertionBoundary and Authority decide what it is worth)
  source_lineage institutional application compiler -- DEFINE, DECLARE, ADDRESS

architecture surface-motif-learning
  canonical_name SurfaceMotifLearning
  historical_name Aurekai
  family surface
  domain Surface / Learning
  layer learning
  semantic_question Which presentation and adjacency motifs recur, and what better candidates should be proposed?
  purpose Learns from action traces and proposes candidates, then proof-gates reversible LOWER/LIFT state through explicit dependency validity envelopes. It proposes and optimizes realization; it never changes deterministic semantic truth.
  maturity implemented
  consumes ActionTrace
  publishes SurfaceCandidate
  forbidden_inference a learned pattern -> changed semantic truth (this organ proposes; the fabric stays authoritative)
  forbidden_inference this organ's former name -> the institution called Aurekai (it held the bare name while owning one learning loop; the institutional world is not an architecture in this registry, and a lookup that returned this entry for that name answered a much larger question with a much smaller organ)
  forbidden_inference a frequent motif -> a correct or authorized one (frequency is not correctness; the fence and Authority still run)
  invariant LOWER requires equivalence evidence and a nonempty invalidation envelope
  invariant a covered dependency change LIFTs the lowered circuit without changing semantic truth
  source_path components/BonfyreControlPlane/pattern_graph.py.archive
  source_path components/BonfyreControlPlane/aurekai_lowering.py.archive
  witness components/BonfyreControlPlane/tests/test_run_history_absorption.py.archive
  witness components/BonfyreControlPlane/tests/test_aurekai_lowering.py.archive
  source_lineage frontend fold -- variation/pattern/promotion above the deterministic fabric
  known_gap M2 builds the reversible control machinery; M9 still owes a real repeated circuit, measured equivalence and dependency-mutation LOWER-to-LIFT proof
  known_gap every source this entry names is archived, so nothing here is a live implementation a reader can open and run. Whether a native owner has taken this work over is not established in this entry; until one is named and witnessed here, the architecture stands on retired code.
architecture market-interface-clones
  canonical_name MarketInterfaceClones
  family surface
  domain Surface / Borrowed interaction
  layer surface
  semantic_question What does a person who has never seen this estate already know how to do here?
  purpose Nine pages that borrow a market interface's behaviour -- the feed, the pin board, the obligation tracker, the stream-and-topic client, the live room, the faceted market, the property search, the federated directory and the territory plane -- and read this estate's own live endpoints through them. What is borrowed is layout, density and gesture. Nothing imports anybody's ontology; the records are the same subjects the rest of the estate addresses.
  maturity implemented
  source_path cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/src/native_publications_query.h
  source_path cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/tests/native_publications_query_test.c
  internal_calculus native donor publication selection materializes the published collection's domain-to-source membership once per query before filtering public observed occurrences
  invariant publication standing, exact source membership, attribution join multiplicity, date and ID ordering, and caller limit remain unchanged when collection membership is materialized
  witness cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/tests/native_publications_query_test.c compares complete ordered rows with the retained correlated query across domain scopes, standing, duplicates, null and numeric selectors and attribution joins; its 2000-occurrence empty-cut fixture reduces SQLite VM work from 6970019 to 37259 steps and passes under ASan/UBSan
  forbidden_inference fewer SQLite VM steps in a publication query -> bounded total page latency, an empty request queue or a production release performance guarantee
  consumes SurfacePattern
  consumes SurfaceIR
  consumes Authority
  publishes ActionTrace
  internal_calculus the donor projects' own front ends, vendored rather than imitated. Each surface loads the donor's real stylesheet from /assets/donor-<project>.css and emits the donor's own DOM, read out of the project's templates: Zulip's message_group/recipient_row/stream_sidebar_row for channels, Pixelfed's TimelineStatus and ServerFeed for discover and community, Pinry's Pins.vue grid for board, Mobilizon's EventView and DateCalendarIcon for stage, Next.js Commerce's grid tile and label for listings. Where the donor needs a build -- Zulip's PostCSS, Mobilizon's and Next.js Commerce's Tailwind -- it is run with the project's own config. Every fetch still resolves to exactly one of three outcomes -- refused, empty, failed -- and each is rendered as a different thing. Every pane names the endpoint that produced it.
  invariant a donor asset carries its attribution header, the project directory it came from under site/matrix/DONOR-LICENSES/, and the commit it was vendored from; that is provenance rather than permission, and a stylesheet with no provenance is a claim nobody can diff, and that is written down instead of quietly reclassified
  invariant a donor asset is versioned by content hash in the URL, so a rebuilt donor is never served from a stale cache while the page that needs it is current
  invariant the estate supplies only what the donor ships and this deployment does not -- its icon font, its avatar service, the media a record never had -- and nothing else is restyled; an override that changes the donor's own rules would make "this is their front end" false
  invariant a surface reads the native owner rather than a CMS type that summarised it; the federation view read a text column saying "73638 peers observed; 57140 shared with hachyderm.io" and now reads /foreign/edges, where from, predicate, to, carrier, observed_at, evidence and claim_state are fields. A surface rendering somebody's sentence is printing a paragraph, not projecting a graph
  invariant a generated field stands where a photograph would and says on the frame that it is generated; a subject that never had a picture does not get one invented for it
  invariant the territory surface borrows nothing, and says why on the page: every donor is one product with one domain, and nothing in the reference estate is shaped like one subject seen four ways
  invariant a surface is a representation and the address is the subject; /s/<kind>/<id> and /room/<kind>/<id> are the same path on every host, because the address belongs to the subject rather than to the territory
  invariant eligibility is per caller, so a page only resolves an address against the host it is standing on; probing another territory anonymously and reporting the result would be showing somebody else's eligibility as this reader's
  invariant a map over a roll with no geometry says so before it draws anything, and uses its projection only for what the roll does carry: lot area at true scale, at the view centre, labelled right size and wrong place
  invariant an avatar's style follows what the subject is: a room, a binary and a federated peer get shapes, an identicon and rings, because a human face on any of them would be the surface asserting a person exists
  invariant the estate carries one mark and one only: Aurekai x Bonfyre as a lockup, a knight on paper beside the wordmark in ink, because the engine and the umbrella are two things and a single badge would say they are one
  invariant the mark is a kit component rather than markup copied into each page; every surface runs a different donor's chrome, so it brings its own scoped styles and depends on no donor class
  invariant a compiled page replaces its wordmark with the lockup rather than joining it; two wordmarks in a row is a merge artefact, not a brand
  invariant the compiled estate loads the same kit the clone surfaces inline, published at the site root because an asset name may not contain a slash -- that guard is the traversal check and is worth more than the tidier path -- and a test holds the two copies identical
  invariant the fifteen commerce stages each name the one owner that can establish them, and the surface marks which the estate actually reaches rather than drawing a bar to the end; a progress bar to Ownership implies every stage from the one that was reached
  invariant non-implication over commerce stages holds across every pair and in both directions, never adjacent ones: the dangerous collapses skip -- paid read as delivered, delivered read as owned -- and an adjacent-only check passes while every one of those goes through
  invariant two commerce stages may involve the same person and never the same owner; an owner is a person at a moment, and collapsing the buyer who assembles a cart with the buyer who reports satisfaction is how a store reads "they added it" as "they were happy with it"
  invariant no stage may be skipped in the other direction either; an exchange reporting delivery with no fulfilment is describing something the estate never saw happen
  invariant Ownership is a .life fact and leaves the store; after a purchase completes the transaction does not stay in .shop
  invariant the four territories differ by ordering principle, not by icon set: .live orders by what is on and lets recency rank, .shop orders by the offer, .life orders by nothing at all, .work orders by what blocks what
  invariant a personal world is never ranked by attention; a kept set sorted by anything is a recommendation feed wearing the clothes of a kept set, and .live is the only territory where now outranks published
  invariant a verb outside its territory is a category error, so every surface takes its verbs from the territory's physics rather than carrying its own list; a mode narrows a territory and never adds a verb the territory does not carry
  invariant the page that shows all four physics quotes the same source the surfaces order by, so the description and the behaviour cannot disagree
  invariant a pattern declares four things and every one is checkable: the owner it reads, the extent it renders at, the action layer it carries and the authority that layer demands
  invariant a pattern reads exactly one owner -- a CMS type or a native organ, never both; a pattern reading both would be two patterns sharing a name, whose human and machine projections could diverge with nothing noticing
  invariant extent decides the action layer: only a page or a workspace carries one, and the catalogue reports no effect class for a chip, card or section rather than trusting the row. A card offering BOOK asks for a decision from a thumbnail
  invariant an unstated extent is treated as permissive rather than as a card; demoting every authored pattern to no-action-layer for a missing column would take the estate's own surfaces down for a migration
  invariant lineage is recorded on each borrowed pattern -- project, files, licence and the commit the asset was vendored from -- which is what makes "only the look was borrowed" a claim somebody can check rather than a slogan
  invariant a declared action layer is what the page actually offers; a verb declared and not rendered, or rendered and not declared, is the declaration becoming decoration
  invariant a 4xx is an answer and not an outage; a pane that treats a refusal as a loading state reports "loading" to a person forever, and every surface here distinguishes refused from empty from failed
  invariant a withheld pane offers the session that would fill it; withholding without offering is a dead end wearing the clothes of a loading state
  invariant one refusal empties one pane and never the page; each pattern is fetched and rendered on its own so a denial is attributable to the pattern that denied
  invariant every pane names the path that produced it; a surface that hides its source cannot be checked against the deployment it claims to describe
  invariant nothing here submits. A verb is rendered as an affordance and Authority gates at effect time, so a chip that posted would be asking for a decision this surface has no standing to carry
  invariant a number computed in the browser names the set it was computed over; a median across one query's rows is not the market, and a page that omits the scope has made a claim the data does not carry
  invariant a surface that is served and unlinked is orphaned rather than shipped; reachability from the authored navigation is part of the deployment, not a follow-up
  forbidden_inference a borrowed layout -> a borrowed ontology (the front end is the donor's, the subjects are this estate's own)
  forbidden_inference an observed edge -> a verified one (claim_state observed means a peer list said so when it was read; the estate has checked nothing)
  forbidden_inference a host named by an edge -> an instance this estate reached (a host may appear only as the far end of somebody else's claim, and the graph marks that as named only)
  forbidden_inference a vendored front end -> the donor project running here (their stylesheet and their DOM, this estate's records and endpoints; none of the donor's backend, data model or ontology is present)
  forbidden_inference a generated field -> a photograph of the subject
  forbidden_inference a reached commerce stage -> any later one (the collapses skip: Product does not establish Ownership, Payment does not establish Delivery, and Delivery does not establish that anybody wanted the contents)
  forbidden_inference an empty carrier -> nothing happened (an empty EPCIS event list means no capture source is admitted, and it says so rather than reading as an absence of movement)
  forbidden_inference four territories carrying different chips -> four sets of physics (the difference that matters is what orders the records, and a shared ordering with different labels is one product wearing four hats)
  forbidden_inference a resolved address -> an authorized one (resolution is eligibility; Authority is checked at effect time by whoever owns the effect)
  forbidden_inference a drawn lot -> a located one (the square is the parcel's real area at the map's real scale, placed at the centre of the view because no source in this estate carries a coordinate)
  forbidden_inference the township's scene -> current state (it is a compiled snapshot and carries the timestamp it was compiled at)
  forbidden_inference an offered verb -> an authorized action
  forbidden_inference a rendered record -> a reservation, an offer accepted, or a completed sale
  forbidden_inference a stage -> a video stream (the live room publishes status, and the surface says so on the stage itself)
  forbidden_inference a capacity note -> current occupancy (it is what the room published, at the time it published it)
  forbidden_inference a read topic -> a handled one (unread state records where a person stopped reading)
  forbidden_inference an unpriced capability -> a free one (no price means nobody has said what it would take)
  forbidden_inference a saved item -> a claim, a commitment, or anybody being told (saving is a note in one browser)
  source_path site/matrix/surfaces/_kit.js
  source_path site/matrix/surfaces/_kit.css
  source_path site/matrix/surfaces/discover.html
  source_path site/matrix/surfaces/board.html
  source_path site/matrix/surfaces/inbox.html
