  source_path site/matrix/surfaces/listings.html
  source_path site/matrix/surfaces/parcels.html
  source_path site/matrix/surfaces/community.html
  source_path site/matrix/surfaces/territory.html
  source_path cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/src/main.c
  witness components/BonfyreControlPlane/tests/clone-surfaces.test.mjs holds all nine against the live deployment on all four hosts: every endpoint each page reads still answers, a gated read is allowed only where the descriptor recorded that it refuses, no page references an asset the organ will not serve, no page submits anything, and each surface carries markers that exist only if its interaction was actually built rather than styled
  witness components/BonfyreControlPlane/tests/territory-surface.test.mjs proves the territory plane projects one subject set into four different field sets rather than four record sets, that .work refuses rather than being empty, and that business mode is ordered by what undoing a move costs rather than by an inventory of installed apps
  source_path site/matrix/donor-zulip.css
  source_path site/matrix/donor-pixelfed.css
  source_path site/matrix/donor-pinry.css
  source_path site/matrix/donor-mobilizon.css
  source_path site/matrix/donor-nextcommerce.css
  source_path site/matrix/donor-maplibre.js
  source_path site/matrix/donor-masonry.js
  source_path site/matrix/surfaces/township.html
  source_path content/habitat
  source_path site/matrix/aurekai-knight.png
  source_path site/matrix/bonfyre-kit.js
  source_path site/matrix/DONOR-LICENSES
  source_path deploy/cms/2026-09-05-surface-pattern-extent-lineage.sql
  witness components/BonfyreControlPlane/tests/commerce-facts.test.mjs checks non-implication over all 105 pairs of the fifteen stages rather than adjacent ones, proves the pairs it names as dangerous actually skip, and holds the live estate to what it reaches: a quote that says it holds nothing, a 402 with facilitator_configured false, an EPCIS event list empty with its reason stated, and an OpenRTB impression list that refuses to invent one
  witness components/BonfyreControlPlane/tests/territory-physics.test.mjs compares each territory's verb list against section 69 exactly, checks that no verb belongs to all four and that each carries one no other does, and proves the orderings produce different orders over the same records rather than the same feed relabelled
  witness components/BonfyreControlPlane/tests/surface-patterns.test.mjs holds every clone to section 68 over its own declaration and over the live catalogue: one owner, an extent from the vocabulary, an action layer only where the extent allows one, an authority statement wherever a verb is offered, the declared verbs actually rendered, and a lineage whose recorded commit matches the vendored asset's
  witness components/BonfyreControlPlane/tests/clone-surfaces.test.mjs also holds the donor claim itself: each surface loads its donor's stylesheet, the estate serves that stylesheet, the page carries the donor's own class names rather than a paraphrase of them, every donor asset carries an attribution header and a licence directory recording which commit was vendored, and every donor URL is versioned by content hash
  source_lineage borrowed interaction -- the front end a person already learned somewhere else, vendored from the project that wrote it, over subjects only this estate has
  known_gap the subject page offers reads and no operations; ObjectGrammar's semantic operations are not yet projected onto it, so a subject is a front door that opens onto a description rather than onto what can be done with the thing
  known_gap the clone surfaces declare themselves as patterns in their own descriptors, and are still deployed as files rather than authored into the CMS surface_pattern catalogue; section 68 says adding a surface should be an authoring act, and for these nine it is a deployment
  known_gap every source in the estate carries Shape.STArea() and Shape.STLength() and no coordinates, so MapLibre has a real basemap and nothing of this estate's own to place on it; the parcels surface states that rather than plotting anything

architecture operator-console
  canonical_name OperatorConsole
  family surface
  domain Surface / Operated
  layer surface
  semantic_question Who decides what this host shows, and how dense it is?
  purpose The surface an institution's own person operates. An institution is a host -- ron.aurekai.work -- so the place where its owner decides which of the estate's patterns appear, at what density, under which mode, above which retention floor, and what of the outside world is admitted, answers at that host's own address. Every one of those decisions is in the URL, which is what makes a shape something a person can hand to someone else rather than a preference kept in one browser.
  maturity implemented
  source_path site/matrix/surfaces/console.html
  source_path site/matrix/surfaces/console.json
  source_path site/matrix/surfaces/_kit.js
  source_path site/matrix/bonfyre-kit.js
  source_path cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/src/main.c
  source_path deploy/cms/2026-09-05-surface-pattern-extent-lineage.sql
  consumes SurfacePattern
  consumes AddressPlane
  consumes ForeignTwin
  consumes Authority
  publishes ActionTrace
  internal_calculus four dials over one Matrix. Extent is served rather than simulated: /_surface/<name>?extent=card is answered by the address organ, which caps the records, reports what it withheld, withholds the effect class, and refuses an extent above the one the pattern was authored at. Mode narrows a territory to one of its six modes and takes its verbs from that mode. Keep is the retention lattice used as an admission floor. The outside is /foreign/edges for what has been observed and /studio/v1/self/foreign/observe for observing one more -- the estate's own ForeignTwin owner, with its robots preflight and its receipt.
  invariant a person gets a host, and a host nobody has created yet still completes TLS; creating an institution cannot require reissuing a certificate, because that is not something an end user can do
  invariant density is a property of the address, not of this browser; the shape is a query string so it can be sent to somebody, and nothing about it is kept in local storage
  invariant one extent for the surface and only the exceptions named; an address that spells out every pattern is correct and unusable
  invariant extent narrows and never grants: a pattern authored at page extent asked for a workspace is refused rather than clamped, because silently serving less than was asked for is how a surface ends up lying about what it is
  invariant the organ withholds the action layer below page extent, not the page; a client that dimmed its own verbs would be a client being polite about a rule
  invariant a narrowed pattern reports the count it withheld; a reference that quietly stopped at its budget would read as the whole set
  invariant a mode's verbs are a subset of its territory's, and every territory verb belongs to at least one of its modes; holding that in both directions is what caught .life carrying no ASSIGN for a household that had chores to give out
  invariant a retention floor hides tiers and says so; that they are not admitted is a different statement from their being empty, and nothing is promoted up the lattice for being popular, referenced or merely surviving
  invariant the outside arrives as edges with receipts and never as sentences; from, predicate, to, carrier, observed_at, evidence and claim_state are fields, and claim_state observed is not a claim about the far side
  invariant the dial reaches the whole estate rather than one page: the compiled pages load their content from the same /_surface/ paths, so the shared chrome mounts the same control and ?x= narrows any of them
  invariant the dial is not drawn where there is nothing to narrow, and does not offer an extent whose only outcome would be a refusal
  cannot_infer shaping a surface -> authority over what it reads; the dials decide what is composed and the effect owner still decides every effect
  cannot_infer a narrowed extent -> a shorter set
  cannot_infer an observed foreign edge -> a connection to that host
  cannot_infer a mode -> a separate product; the six modes are projections of one Matrix, and a fifth territory would duplicate it
  cannot_infer a retention floor -> those tiers being empty
  witness components/BonfyreControlPlane/tests/operator-console.test.mjs holds the four dials against the live deployment: that ron.aurekai.work resolves to person:ron and a host nobody has created still completes TLS while the apexes keep their own certificate, that each extent caps the records and reports what it withheld, that the organ withholds the effect class below page extent and refuses an extent above the authored one, that every mode's verbs are a subset of its territory's and together exhaust it, that the retention lattice is in section 61's order and no tier is inferred from traffic, that the foreign graph is edges rather than prose and observing without a session is refused, and that the shape lives in the address rather than in local storage
  known_gap the shape is addressable but not saved: a person who wants their host to open at their shape has to keep the URL, because the console writes no institution_surface row and the estate has no per-caller default surface yet
  known_gap the retention tier of a pattern is a table in the kit rather than a field on the pattern; it belongs on surface_pattern next to extent, where a CMS write would set it
  known_gap /console is the same page for a signed-in owner and a stranger; a host's own person and a visitor to that host should not be offered the same dials, and nothing here distinguishes them yet

interaction console-turns-extent-on-patterns
  source operator-console
  destination surface-pattern
  relation narrows
  preserves the record set's order and the identity of every record it does render
  preserves the pattern's declaration of what it reads and the authority it demands
  drops the records past the extent's budget, and reports how many
  drops the effect class below page extent, with the reason in the answer
  forbidden_inference a narrowed pattern -> a pattern with fewer records
  forbidden_inference an extent -> an authority; narrowing changes what is composed and never who may act

interaction console-reads-the-address-plane
  source operator-console
  destination address-plane
  relation projects
  preserves the host's institution, territory, audience and world as the address organ resolved them
  preserves eligibility as a per-caller fact; the console shows this reader's host and never probes another to report somebody else's
  drops nothing of the coordinate; the shape is added to the address rather than replacing any of it
  forbidden_inference a host answering -> an institution with anything to show
  forbidden_inference a shape in the address -> a shape the estate has stored

architecture surface-renderer
  canonical_name SurfaceRenderer
  family surface
  domain Surface / Interaction grammar
  layer surface
  semantic_question What is the human grammar of this surface, separately from what it happens to be reading?
  purpose The abstraction that was missing while route, SurfacePattern, renderer and data source were one thing. A renderer is the interaction language on its own -- Pinry's masonry, Zulip's stream-to-topic keyboard, Next.js Commerce's facet rail and compare tray, Plane's obligation density -- and it reads nothing. That is what lets one grammar carry a different owner without being rebuilt, and what turns nine deployed routes from nine products into nine reusable languages.
  maturity implemented
  source_path cmd/BonfyreCMS/content-types/surface_renderer.json
  source_path site/matrix/surfaces/_kit.js
  source_path cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/src/main.c
  consumes SurfacePattern
  publishes SurfaceIR
  internal_calculus eleven renderers authored as CMS rows and served at /_surface/renderers, each naming its grammar, the seam where protocol affordances attach, what it can render, the extents it works at and what it must not be read to imply. Watch is a media presentation grammar over MediaProgram; it is distinct from the filesystem BonfyreWatch organ. The pattern still reads exactly one owner; the renderer names no owner at all, and the two halves are checked against each other rather than trusted.
  invariant a renderer names no owner; one that reads something has become a pattern, and the grammar is welded to a source again
  invariant a pattern names no grammar; one that describes a facet rail has absorbed the renderer, and the two can then disagree about what a surface is
  invariant lineage survives extraction: the donor a grammar came from is recorded on the renderer, and the two renderers that borrow nothing say so rather than being given one
  invariant a route that held two grammars yields two renderers; extracting one from /parcels would have trapped the map canvas inside property search forever
  invariant a renderer declares its extents from the same vocabulary a pattern does, so a grammar cannot claim a density the estate has no word for
  invariant every deployed route keeps working; phase one preserves the surfaces and only makes their grammar portable
  cannot_infer a renderer -> a projection; it renders what a pattern resolved and resolves nothing itself
  cannot_infer a grammar borrowed from a donor -> the donor's ontology, backend or data model
  cannot_infer a renderer being able to render a pattern -> that pattern being served on this host
  witness components/BonfyreControlPlane/tests/surface-renderers.test.mjs holds the seam open from both sides: that the ten renderers are authored rather than compiled, that each states a grammar, a seam, what it renders and what it cannot infer, that no renderer names a CMS type or an organ binary and no pattern describes an interaction, that the donor lineage survived, that /parcels yielded two renderers rather than one, and that the view control reaches a compiled estate page
  known_gap a renderer cannot yet be pointed at a pattern it was not extracted with; VIEW_ROUTE maps each grammar to the one route it lives at, so the portability is declared and the composition that would use it is unbuilt
  known_gap the nine clone surfaces inline the kit rather than loading it, so they carry no view control; only the compiled estate, the console and the link desk have one

architecture census-reader
  canonical_name CensusReader
  family surface
  domain Surface / Contract interpretation
  layer surface
  semantic_question Who is allowed to decide what a census row means?
  purpose The census puts the extraction contract on the row so that no page knows PeerTube calls it thumbnailPath and Lemmy calls it thumbnail_url. That holds only while one thing reads the contract. It had grown three readers -- the landing wall, the operator console, the world reader -- and they had already disagreed: one honoured is_nsfw and the others did not, one could complete a federated image path and the others could not, one fell back to a feed's guid for the outward link and the others dropped the link. Three readers of one contract is three places to be wrong about the same source, and the census stops being the place that decides.
  maturity implemented
  source_path site/matrix/surfaces/_kit.js
  consumes InternetCensus
  publishes DerivedView
  internal_calculus K.readSource fetches the retained bytes for a row's twin, branches once on whether the contract is a feed selector or a JSON path, and completes the row's fields: the item list, the title, the meta, the outward link, who made it, and the picture. An image path that is not absolute is completed the way the row says -- an @field naming the host that made the item, a pre|post pair wrapping an identifier, or a fixed origin.
  invariant one interpreter; a surface that reads /foreign/body and maps the fields itself has copied the contract out of the census
  invariant an empty extract means the body is itself the list, and that is the only field where blank carries meaning; it is written down where the reading happens rather than assumed in three places
  invariant a source's own adult or sensitive flag is honoured, and honouring it is reading a field rather than editorial judgement
  invariant the reader names no source and no host; the moment it knows one by name the census has a rival
  cannot_infer retained bytes -> a live source; this parses what was kept under a receipt, and an empty result means this estate read nothing rather than that the source published nothing
  cannot_infer a rendered item -> a licence to redistribute it; the picture stays where it lives and this holds the address
  witness components/BonfyreControlPlane/tests/worlds.test.mjs checks the interpreter is in the kit, that no surface carries a second one, and that every field the census authors is actually read by it
  known_gap the nine clone surfaces inline the kit rather than loading it, so a change to the interpreter reaches them only when they are rebuilt

architecture subject-index
  canonical_name SubjectIndex
  family surface
  domain Surface / Compression
  layer surface
  semantic_question What is this subject, everywhere at once?
  purpose The read the estate did not have. It held 326 subjects, 274 addresses and 319 presences and could enumerate none of them, so every surface started from a pattern -- a list of records of one type -- which is the separate-social-object, separate-market-object, separate-work-object shape the compression law exists to forbid. This answers the other question: one addressed subject, its addresses, and the territory / scope / world / representation it is projected into.
  maturity implemented
  source_path cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/src/main.c
  source_path site/matrix/surfaces/console.html
  consumes AddressPlane
  publishes DerivedView
  internal_calculus /subjects lists every subject with its address, presence and relation counts; naming one returns its constellation. The console draws it as a matrix of territory against representation, so a subject in four territories is one row of cells rather than four objects.
  invariant one index and not an ours half and a theirs half; a foreign twin is a subject beside an institution, which is what makes reverse federation structural rather than a feature
  invariant the index stays a list until a subject is named; a constellation per row would be quadratic and would also answer a question nobody asked
  invariant a subject offers something readable: an id is a digest for most kinds, and eighty-four rows of budgetrequest:01135de0 is a list nobody can use even though the estate knew an address for every one of them
  cannot_infer a presence -> a permission; that a subject is projected into market scope says the estate projects it there, never that this caller may read or act on it
  cannot_infer an address existing -> a surface answering at it
  witness components/BonfyreControlPlane/tests/surface-renderers.test.mjs checks the index answers for every kind, that foreign twins and institutions share one list, that naming a subject returns its projections with the counts agreeing, and that an unnamed listing carries no constellation

architecture foreign-link-desk
  canonical_name ForeignTwinWorkspace
  family surface
  domain Surface / External Estate
  layer surface
  semantic_question Which external source contracts can participate in Aurekai, what has each actually reached, and what remains only a proposal?
  purpose The public Links, Sources and ForeignTwin routes use the native Source Desk. The shared bounded collection supplies search, inspection, accessible tabs, commands and resizable panes. Retained passages can be reviewed into an installed research workspace through its current destination and record owners. Publication and lost-response recovery remain with the atomic SourceCollection/World owner. link.html is a retained compatibility carrier, not the current public route renderer.
  maturity implemented
  source_path cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/src/source_desk.h
  source_path cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/src/publication_retained.h
  source_path schemas/control/publication-occurrence.cue
  source_path integrations/browser/publication-picker.mjs
  source_path integrations/browser/publication-research.mjs
  source_path integrations/browser/source-desk.mjs
  source_path integrations/browser/source-desk.css
  source_path integrations/browser/workspace-destinations.mjs
  invariant the shared research dialog accepts an exact private source-set reference as well as public retained-reader coordinates; its saved-source adapter rereads the record and checks selected passages before preparing or saving, without replacing the original selection
  witness cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/tests/connections_workspace.test.mjs proves the saved-source adapter retains exact text and receipts, refuses source corrections and a deleted selection, and recovers a committed research record after a lost reply
  source_path integrations/browser/interaction-collection.mjs
  source_path scripts/tests/source-desk-browser.test.mjs
  source_path scripts/tests/source-publication-browser.test.mjs
  source_path site/matrix/surfaces/link.html
  source_path site/matrix/surfaces/link.json
  source_path site/matrix/surfaces/build/link_workspace_test.sh
  source_path components/BonfyreProject/tests/foreign_release_projection_test.sh
  source_path cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/src/main.c
  source_path cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/tests/auth_surface_test.sh
  source_path cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/tests/world_native_material_test.sh
  consumes ForeignTwin
  consumes Authority
  publishes ForeignOccurrence
  internal_calculus /foreign/twins is a paginated source-release catalogue built in bounded scans over published source contracts, SourceFrontier, ItemArchive and authored SiteProgram←SourceCollection←source_refs, with an exact-address frontier join and a second exact-source index for archive/economic reductions; it does not enumerate the 135k-row receipt directory. Every page carries offset/limit/total/estate_total/next_offset while its release_summary remains whole-estate. A q parameter is only a literal authored-contract filter and is debounced in the workspace; it cannot pretend to rank relevance or transform the whole-estate summary. Its stage tuple is source contract, frontier admission, archive material, program-input binding with delivery state not_verified, authored spatial/media/rights/publisher extraction facets, exact-source economic observations and readiness paths. Exact receipt chronology remains separately queryable.
  invariant the workspace reads a source release only from existing owners; the renderer never infers a public program from SourceFrontier admission, ItemArchive depth, a family, or a selected destination
  invariant compatibility-carrier source comparisons and destination choices are bounded transient presentation state; source, subject, URL and catalogue generation remain distinct; TSV reference export and comparison never activate a destination; no new persistent browser distribution-plan sidecar is written
  invariant a selected ForeignTwin may publish only explicit typed SourceCollection then World CMS owners through the authenticated CMS write surface; the collection receives the exact source_refs selection and PublicationOccurrence material_kind, the person supplies title, lede and character, and the World binds source_collection:<id>; native composition resolves only a published named collection that explicitly declares PublicationOccurrence and only material already lawful for its exact sources, without admitting material, assigning contributors, establishing an institution, claiming a provider, granting data-combination rights, authority, payment, or external effect
  invariant an economic destination is a request for an evidence-bound quote or offer comparison and is never rendered as a price, payment, purchase, funding commitment, or settlement
  invariant the workspace calls a path ready only when the exact upstream owner inputs exist; readiness never upgrades a declared extractor, price observation, claim, account link, or proposed destination into a derived fact, active program, offer, route, authority, or external control
  invariant the workspace loads the first bounded rich page and explicit later pages; it reports loaded versus total rather than representing the initial slice as the whole external estate
  invariant explicit next pages and selected comparisons retain catalogue_generation; changed generations hold selected identities for review instead of blending releases; failed pages retain their cursor for deliberate retry and obsolete requests cannot replace a newer selection
  invariant the release catalogue reports the price ledger's exact source-contract alignment separately, so an unbound economic observation cannot appear under an unrelated source merely because both describe the same market
  invariant a geographic destination is proposed only; a source-labelled place does not become a spatially valid local projection without a spatial owner witness
