architecture pack-graph
  source_path cmd/BonfyreCMS/tests/program_continuation_test.c
  source_path cmd/BonfyreCMS/tests/program_continuation_test.mk
  source_path cmd/BonfyreCMS/tests/program_continuation_test.md
  witness cmd/BonfyreCMS/tests/program_continuation_test.c admits a second pack through actual CMS plan, install and activate commands, then checks native ExternalEstate public forwarding includes its explicit public activation, excludes private actor and pack-lock coordinates, preserves both activation records and leaves scoped native resolution active; the five-check PACK_LOCK_ADVERTISEMENT_PASS marker is separate from the six continuation checks and both groups pass under ASan/UBSan
  canonical_name PackGraph
  family surface
  domain Surface / Behaviour
  layer surface
  semantic_question What behaviour is running here, who published it, and what did it change?
  purpose The organ that made the estate product-thin without making it capability-thin. The native kernel is still the whole mature estate -- AddressPlane, authority, evidence, finance, WorkGraph, ForeignTwins, the command contracts, the model estate, the protocol machinery. What left it is the branch per product. A pack is an addressed behaviour artifact, and food, dating, grant readiness, lease search, a night out, a loss programme and a motorcycle club are now compositions over the machine rather than conditions inside it.
  maturity implemented
  source_path cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/src/main.c
  source_path cmd/BonfyreCMS/content-types/pack_artifact.json
  source_path cmd/BonfyreCMS/content-types/pack_version.json
  source_path cmd/BonfyreCMS/content-types/pack_head.json
  source_path cmd/BonfyreCMS/content-types/pack_dependency.json
  source_path cmd/BonfyreCMS/content-types/pack_overlay.json
  source_path cmd/BonfyreCMS/content-types/pack_installation.json
  source_path cmd/BonfyreCMS/content-types/pack_activation.json
  source_path cmd/BonfyreCMS/content-types/pack_demand.json
  source_path site/matrix/surfaces/packs.html
  source_path site/matrix/surfaces/packs.json
  source_path cmd/BonfyreExternalEstate/src/main.c
  consumes AddressPlane
  consumes Authority
  consumes SurfacePattern
  consumes ForeignTwin
  publishes SurfaceIR
  internal_calculus a closure is resolved per actor: activations are gathered, dependencies closed to a bounded depth, overlays applied in composition order, and the result is the smallest sufficient set of packs with the views it asks for, the external reality it needs, the capabilities it wants and the policy its overlays tightened to. Versions are addressed by a digest over the pack's own identity, dependencies, demands and overlays, so two packs claiming to be the same is checkable.
  invariant five things never merge: a subject, an institution, a pack, an internet cut and a surface. The moment a pack is an identity it can grant itself authority, and the moment a community is a pack it cannot fork one
  invariant an overlay may only hide, add, specialize, present, tighten or default; the list is closed and has no verb for granting authority, widening disclosure, rewriting identity, dropping evidence or promoting an observation to a fact
  invariant an overlay using a verb outside that list is reported as refused rather than dropped, because a silently ignored override is a community believing it configured something it did not
  invariant a published overlay with no target is refused before native string matching; refusal serialization is bounded and preserves valid JSON even when many overlays are malformed
  invariant a tighten narrows and never widens; a later layer may narrow further and can never undo what an earlier one narrowed
  invariant composition order binds official, then institution, then community, then household, then scenario, and every level has something in it -- a precedence rule with an empty level is a rule nobody has tested
  invariant forking is not installing, installing is not activating, and activating is not authorizing; the four counts differ in the live graph and a closure is built from activations alone
  invariant a pack refers to shared bases rather than containing copies; five community packs over one base are one base and five sparse overlays
  invariant a scenario is temporary configuration asked for at the time, never an installation and never an institution
  invariant a dependency cycle is bounded rather than hung; an authoring error is an authoring error and not an outage
  invariant a pack declares demand and does not fetch; the body regime is REMOTE unless a claim depends on the bytes
  cannot_infer an activated pack -> an authorized effect; a closure decides what is composed and offers verbs, and Authority decides every effect at effect time
  cannot_infer a pack -> an identity; it holds no authority and no state and no host resolves to one
  cannot_infer a resolved closure -> permission to read what it composes
  cannot_infer a hidden view -> a pattern that stopped answering; hiding is presentation and a machine asking for it gets the same bytes
  cannot_infer a declared demand -> retained bytes
  cannot_infer a forwarded activation -> a resolved closure, an applied overlay or an authorized verb; the forwarding cut narrows which packs are worth composing and composition and Authority still happen afterwards
  cannot_infer a compiled demand coordinate -> a scheduled hydration; ResourceWeather still does not read pack demand, and an emitted declaration is not a fetch, a reservation or permission to retrieve a body
  witness components/BonfyreControlPlane/tests/pack-graph.test.mjs runs the architecture test against the deployment: that no product name appears as a condition in the organ, that a community fork keeps its parent as a dependency rather than copying it, that the verb list is closed and contains nothing that widens, that every internet demand is REMOTE and carries a reheat condition, that a pack is not an addressable subject, that a scenario has no institution and does not persist after being asked for, that an installation does not resolve into a closure, that Ron is offered neither vertical nor stage, that a community's own overlays apply under a governed head, and that two actors get demonstrably different products from one engine
  witness cmd/BonfyreExternalEstate/tests/external_estate_test.sh compiles published activations and declared demand into the shared forwarding index and proves the plane can ask which packs are live for a scope before any overlay is composed: an activation carries its pack, subject, scope and conditions plus a dependency edge on every pack head it declares, a publish of the parent head retires the fork's activation cut through PackGraph:activation, and a declared demand carries its kind, needs, preferred sources, fields, body regime and reheat condition
  known_gap the nine absorbed Frappe lineages are declared as dependencies and authored as packs by nobody, so a closure that names them resolves past them silently; the edge is recorded and the target is not
  known_gap PackIR exists only as the digest: there is no dense runtime image, no BFP section and no delta upgrade, so a pack is compact because it is small rather than because it was compiled
  known_gap a head advances by an authoring act and the governance rule is a sentence on the artifact; nothing enforces the quorum it names
  known_gap ResourceWeather does not read pack demand yet, so nothing schedules hydration against it; the demand is declared and the scheduler that would consume it is unbuilt

architecture internet-commons
  canonical_name InternetCommons
  family surface
  domain Surface / External world
  layer surface
  semantic_question Where does the outside world live, if not inside this estate?
  purpose A remote public world rather than a mirror. The four territory hosts under internet.aurekai.* are where external material is addressed, and the default physical state is identity, a digest, typed relations, a source passport and a receipt -- not a copy of the site. Retention is a ladder, and most of it should sit near the bottom.
  maturity declared
  source_path cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/src/main.c
  source_path site/matrix/surfaces/link.html
  consumes ForeignTwin
  publishes ForeignOccurrence
  internal_calculus eight hosts now resolve -- four for the commons that publishes packs, four territories for the internet institution -- and the retention ladder is stated on the pack surface against the demand a closure actually declares. The observing half is built: receipts, retained bodies, cooling. The cut is addressed and its shape is declared.
  invariant meaning and reproducibility are retained; unnecessary bytes are not
  invariant a body moves up the ladder because a claim depends on it, never because a source was seen
  invariant an internet cut is not a pack and not an institution; it is where external material is addressed
  cannot_infer an observed source -> a claim about it
  cannot_infer a candidate address -> a subject this estate has resolved
  known_gap the ladder is described and enforced by nothing: there is no L0/L1/L2 field on a twin, so where a twin actually sits is inferred from whether a body happens to be on disk
  known_gap the vertical hosts -- food, housing, grants, bishop, creators, reviews -- have not been evaluated one by one; the target is a cut plus a pack for the ones that are categories and a promotion for the ones that are institutions

interaction closure-selects-renderers
  source pack-graph
  destination surface-renderer
  relation selects
  preserves the renderer's own grammar and its lineage; a closure asks for a view and implements none of it
  preserves the refusal; a view a closure does not ask for is unlit with the reason stated
  drops nothing of the registry; the closure narrows what is offered and never what exists
  forbidden_inference a view offered by a closure -> a pattern that answers on this host
  forbidden_inference a hidden view -> a withdrawn projection

interaction closure-declares-internet-demand
  source pack-graph
  destination internet-commons
  relation demands
  preserves the demand as declared: what is needed, from which sources, which fields, at which body regime, and when it should be reheated
  drops the fetching; a pack declares and never observes, and the ForeignTwin owner is the only thing that reads a source
  forbidden_inference a declared demand -> an observation
  forbidden_inference a preferred source -> a source this estate has permission to read

architecture territory-landing
  canonical_name TerritoryLanding
  family surface
  domain Surface / Arrival
  layer surface
  semantic_question What does a stranger see, and what makes the rest worth an account?
  purpose The public arrival aperture. It removes the dashboard/capability catalogue and begins with a usable bounded operation: submit one public URL to the native intake owner, which prepares a reviewable route but does not observe, retain, publish, or claim it. Life, Live, Shop, and Work retain distinct visual character and wording, then open the existing Discover, Market, Studio, and native session owners rather than reimplementing them. A small public weather-carrier indicator proves the page can respond to the outside without retaining a source body or inventing a weather claim.
  maturity implemented
  source_path site/matrix/surfaces/home.json
  source_path site/matrix/surfaces/home.html
  source_path site/matrix/surfaces/build/mk_home.py.archive
  source_path cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/src/main.c
  source_path cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/src/territory_home.c
  source_path cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/src/public_home_search.c
  consumes SurfaceIR
  consumes AddressPlane
  consumes ForeignTwin
  publishes ActionTrace
  internal_calculus one authored page has host-scoped presentation lowered by WebAddress for four territory characters. Its first form is a same-origin GET to /_surface/intake with one URL; the intake owner returns route preparation. A second HTMX form asks the native /_surface/external-estate for public observations without a browser-owned search application. Three cards link to existing owners; the sign-in door uses the native session owner. The weather indicator requests /_surface/home-weather as a small owner-rendered HTML fragment.
  invariant four hosts differ in visual character, question and immediate framing; a single palette swap is not territory-specific arrival
  invariant both public forms are owner-backed GET apertures; neither fetches a submitted foreign URL, retains a body, or submits an observe/publish/effect operation
  invariant account state remains owned by native session verification, never localStorage bearer recovery
  invariant the weather indicator renders only owner-returned public carrier availability; it never asserts a condition, forecast, provider admission, or retained body
  invariant a machine asking for the root still gets the discovery descriptor; authoring a route never takes away a machine contract the route already had
  invariant a machine asking for the root still gets the native discovery descriptor; the human page cannot replace the machine contract
  cannot_infer a submitted public URL -> evidence, ForeignTwin, canonical truth, relationship, provider availability, or authority over the foreign system
  cannot_infer a public carrier availability count -> current weather, forecast correctness, a retained body, or an admitted provider
  cannot_infer a door into Discover, Market, Studio, or account -> read/write/effect permission
  witness cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/tests/auth_surface_test.sh proves browser cookie session transport remains native, read-only, revocable, and distinct from any institution grant; cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/tests/web_address_test.sh proves root machine discovery is preserved
  known_gap the public weather card reads the already-existing owner endpoint and has no independently recorded browser-surface witness yet; it must not be promoted from implemented visual integration to measured public rollout until that witness runs against a deployed host
  invariant a URL submitted without a discovery coordinate opens a URL review; an explicitly supplied occurrence, including an empty one, remains subject to the existing exact candidate-pair check
  invariant reviewing a URL performs no fetch; the existing native ForeignTwin POST remains behind session and write-scope checks; sign-in continuation preserves the URL including encoded query characters
  witness cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/tests/url_review.test.mjs verifies anonymous, read-only and write-authorized review, candidate refusal, escaped input, complete sign-in continuation after failure and success, and an explicit authorized read retained by the native observer
  witness packs/no-simulation/home-contract-20261013/browser.json checks four native territory fallback pages at desktop and phone widths and follows intake through URL review without fetching the supplied external address
  known_gap the live apex front pages currently use PageComposition, while this fallback template shares one visual layout across territory classes; the fallback browser witness does not establish distinct visual characters or a public rollout of URL review

interaction landing-prepares-native-public-route
  source territory-landing
  destination surface-ir
  relation bounded-owner-aperture
  preserves controlled-host territory character, one user-proposed public URL, public observation-search query, native session door, owner route coordinates, and public weather-carrier availability only
  drops submitted foreign response bodies, ForeignTwin admission, provider credentials, browser bearer storage, authority grants, account details, weather assertions, settlement, publication, and every external effect
