architecture internet-census
  canonical_name InternetCensus
  family surface
  domain Surface / External world
  layer surface
  semantic_question What are all the ways the outside world can tell this estate something, and which of them is worth reading again?
  purpose Not a list of integrations. A map of every useful way the outside world can say what exists, what changed, what is hot, what is nearby, what is available, what is for sale, what people are discussing, what machines advertise and what may be acted on -- with an access label on each, and, for the few that have actually been pointed at, the twin holding the receipt and the contract for reading what came back.
  maturity implemented
  source_path cmd/BonfyreCMS/content-types/internet_source.json
  source_path cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/src/main.c
  source_path components/BonfyreProject/src/main.c
  source_path deploy/systemd/bonfyre-reheat.service
  source_path deploy/systemd/bonfyre-reheat.timer
  source_path site/matrix/surfaces/home.html
  consumes ForeignTwin
  consumes PackDemand
  publishes ForeignOccurrence
  internal_calculus two hundred and twenty two rows: two hundred families declared and deliberately unwalked, eighteen concrete sources observed on a schedule, four refused and frozen. Each observed row carries an extraction contract -- which path holds the items, which field is the title, which field is the number -- so a surface reads a source it has never heard of without knowing its shape. Reheating is scheduled by ResourceWeather: the source's own cadence, multiplied by a tier, promoted by pack demand, demoted by silence, frozen by a refusal.
  invariant the census is a map and not a walk; most of it is declared and unobserved on purpose, and an estate that has observed most of its own census is mirroring the internet slowly
  invariant the extraction contract lives on the row rather than in a page; eighteen source shapes compiled into a landing page is the branch-per-product shape one layer up
  invariant the timer is a heartbeat and the cadence is in the data; a source with a six-hour cadence is asked every six hours however often the timer wakes
  invariant a refusal freezes rather than being retried; robots_disallow is an answer, and asking again every five minutes is not persistence
  invariant a source no activated pack's demand names falls a tier each time it is passed over, and stops being read at all
  invariant a receipt file is a history, one observation per line; reading it from the start answers with the first time a source was ever seen, which is the wrong body the moment anything is reheated
  invariant the scheduler is the organ that already owns the store, not a script beside it; two programs with two ideas of what a receipt looks like is one of them being wrong quietly
  invariant the scheduler writes nothing back to the census: the row is authored intent -- the url, the cadence, the contract -- and when a source was last read is a fact already in its own receipt
  invariant the tier is derived each run rather than stored; the authored tier is a floor, the last observation is the standing, and an activated pack's demand promotes
  invariant a says line is written in words a stranger knows, because the census is what the landing page speaks with
  invariant a media source carries where the picture is, how to get out to it and who made it; a wall that knows PeerTube calls it thumbnailPath and Lemmy calls it thumbnail_url is a wall with the outside world compiled into it
  invariant a relative thumbnail resolves against the host that made it, not the host that answered; a federated search returns video from many instances and one fixed origin breaks every one of them
  invariant a picture that will not load is removed rather than left as a placeholder; a grey rectangle sitting on a readable caption is worse than the caption alone
  invariant things you can look at come before columns of words; a trending tag is a word about the visible world and a thumbnail is the visible world
  cannot_infer a reheated source -> a fresh fact; the receipt says when it was read, not that what it says is true
  cannot_infer a declared family -> a source this estate can reach
  cannot_infer an access label -> permission; a label says what kind of thing the source offers, never that this estate may take it
  cannot_infer a retained body -> redistribution rights
  witness components/BonfyreControlPlane/tests/internet-census.test.mjs holds the local native scheduler, receipt and public-page invariants; opt-in BONFYRE_LIVE_WITNESS=1 or BONFYRE_LIVE_BASE_URL also checks that the census remains mostly unobserved, that observed and refused rows carry the right contracts, that published weather paces reads, and that retained bytes and media remain reachable by twin
  known_gap the two hundred families are names and labels; none carries a concrete endpoint, so a pack asking for one of them has nothing to bind to yet
  known_gap demand promotion matches on words, so a family called "attention" is not matched by a pack demanding "Recipe" even when the recipe world is exactly what that attention source would serve
  known_gap the media is a thumbnail and a link out, never an embedded player; nothing here streams, and the video is watched at the instance that holds it
  known_gap only the fediverse answers with pictures and no key -- PeerTube, Lemmy, NASA. The platforms that hold most of the visible social world are in the census as families and need partner access this estate does not have
  known_gap WebSub subscription and coalesced SourceDirty drain are native and receipt-bound; firehose and general webhook families remain unbound, and no candidate census row is subscribed merely because it advertises push
  known_gap the reheat still runs from a systemd timer rather than from the organ's own loop, so the estate depends on the host's scheduler to breathe; the decision of what to read is native and the heartbeat is not

