architecture presentation-template
  canonical_name PresentationTemplate
  family surface
  domain Surface / Design language
  layer surface
  semantic_question What does this look like, asked separately from what it is and what it reads?
  purpose The third axis. A world already had a character -- what elements exist -- and a set of grammars -- what interactions it descends into. Neither answers what the page looks like, and folding the look into the character makes the equation fifteen worlds equals fifteen designs, then two hundred and thirty-eight themes equals two hundred and thirty-eight sites. A template is a design language on its own: type, colour, density, card and hero policy, expressed as the same named roles every character already declares. Seven characters against six templates is forty-two looks over one reader, and neither axis was told about the other.
  maturity implemented
  source_path cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/src/site_presentation.c
  source_path cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/src/site_presentation.h
  witness cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/tests/site_product_test.sh exercises native customer presentation updates, homepage and standing/contact-page parity, cross-customer isolation and rejection of injected CSS, unknown roles, invalid modes and foreign font hosts
  invariant native site rendering lowers the same published template through a shared closed-role reader; site set --presentation changes only a customer-owned template and validates the full patch before the CMS write
  source_path cmd/BonfyreCMS/content-types/presentation_template.json
  source_path components/BonfyreServiceSite/training-presentation.mjs
