  publishes DerivedView
  internal_calculus six templates authored as CMS rows and served at /_surface/presentation-templates, each carrying a layout_tokens object over a closed list of presentation roles -- ground, ink, display, accent, muted, rule, panel, three faces, the display metrics, radius, card border and shadow, gap and measure. The reader resolves a template from the address first and the authored world second, parses the tokens, and sets them inline on the body so no selector has to out-specify another. A role a template does not mention keeps the character's own.
  invariant a template reads no owner and holds no subject state; one that names a content type, an organ or a subject has stopped being a way of looking and become a thing looked at
  invariant the reader applies only roles it declared; an open-ended token bag would let a row reach past presentation into the layout the character owns
  invariant the character is the fallback and not a second opinion; every resolution failure returns nothing and the page renders whole under the character's own defaults, because a template that half-applies is worse than one that does not apply
  invariant a template loads the faces it names; only one font host is reachable from these pages, so a face named and not loaded renders in the fallback stack and the language is quietly not the language
  invariant the page declares which template it is wearing beside which character it is, as data-template and data-character markup rather than visible copy; a maintainer who cannot tell them apart cannot tell which one to blame, and a reader should never have to
  invariant provenance is recorded and is not a dependency; reference_source and reference_name say where a language was studied, and no third-party theme code runs here
  cannot_infer a template -> the publication it was studied from; wearing a newsroom's typography does not make anything on the page reported, edited or filed
  cannot_infer a design language -> a claim about the material; confidence, urgency and authority are typographic choices this estate made and say nothing about how sure anybody is of what is written
  cannot_infer a template applying -> a template being appropriate; the address will dress any world in any language, and nothing checks that the result is honest
  witness components/BonfyreControlPlane/tests/worlds.test.mjs checks that no template names a content type or an organ, that each carries its reference and a parseable token object covering every colour role, that each loads the faces it names, that no two are the same language by ground, accent and display face together, that the address beats the authored template, that every failure path in the resolver returns nothing, and that each character still declares its own ground so it can stand alone
  witness 2026-09-29 the Bun palette compiler reproduced all 1,152 prior Python rows exactly after the intentional reference URL move, and compile_palette_profiles.test.mjs verifies eight families, closed roles and reference-candidate status
  known_gap the template is chosen and never checked; acceptance_contract is authored prose that nothing evaluates, so a world can wear a language whose contract its material does not satisfy
  known_gap the older authored six are now joined by a compiled Ghost reference census of two hundred and thirty-eight, but presentation selection has not yet evaluated a material's actual acceptance contract
  known_gap native customer home, standing and contact pages now consume closed typography, layout and mode roles; other legacy surfaces still carry independent looks. The service-site kit consumes authored template roles at build time
  known_gap 2026-10-12 site/matrix/aurekai-bar.css also carries a layer over the surfaces laid out by borrowed sheets (boards, schedule, community, listings); it is keyed on the presence of a donor stylesheet link and forces ground, faces and scale with !important, so a donor sheet update can break it silently and nothing tests it
  known_gap 2026-10-12 site/matrix/world.css, matrix.css and aurekai-site-program.css each end with one estate dress whose selectors outrank the per-region and per-section template styles on the four territories' own pages, their rooms and member addresses; the template rows are still resolved and emitted, but their colour and face roles no longer show there. Independent customer sites keep their own templates. The override is a stylesheet layer, not a selection rule in the template reader
  cannot_infer a data-bf-profile attribute on a territory, room or member page -> that the page is drawn in that template; since 2026-10-12 those pages share one dress and the attribute records only which row was resolved
