  consumes WorldPublication
  consumes SurfaceIR
  consumes PackGraph
  consumes CapabilityClosure
  publishes SurfaceCompositionIR
  invariant a selected Ghost profile changes page presentation and slot geometry only; it never changes subject identity, source admission, rights, audience, authority or effects
  invariant a SiteProgram applies only the closed CSS token set from its selected published PresentationTemplate; a reference-candidate Ghost census row is not live art direction, and a token cannot inject a selector, URL, script or a declaration outside the named composition variables
  invariant SitePresentation navigation names generated SurfaceProgram grammars rather than URLs; an unknown grammar is omitted instead of becoming a caller-authored route
  invariant a SiteProgram loads a donor stylesheet only when a published ApplicationBinding selects a lowerer that declares that asset; the global renderer registry is not site chrome
  invariant apparent page blocks lower only real typed material or typed applications; raw source IDs, protocol labels and ExperienceChain prose are forbidden public content
  invariant SiteProgram composes through SitePresentation instead of restating subject, territory or GhostProfile; changing art direction never silently mutates semantic identity or the external candidate reservoir
  invariant native /_surface/site-program resolves one published SiteProgram through its published SitePresentation and returns typed composition references only; it never returns raw source descriptors, protocol labels, authority or effects
  invariant a matching published SitePresentation host owns its apex human document before legacy donor/static fallback; unknown hosts continue to their existing AddressPlane path; a territory's own apex (aurekai.live, .life, .shop, .work) is not an institution site and opens on its PageComposition front page first
  invariant a published WorkExample projects only where its exact profile-site coordinate matches; a global territory listing and an unbound row never become public released work
  invariant a released WorkExample's primary action enters /programs in the visitor's own destination with its program_template; setting up the underlying tool alone stays a secondary link, and an unmigrated store reads the release as unbound rather than hiding it
  invariant an anonymous SiteProgram response is a derived public closure product whose cache dependencies are the exact SiteProgram, SitePresentation, SemanticSlot and ApplicationBinding coordinates emitted to AddressPlane; bearer-bearing requests never enter that cache
  invariant a source collection is a reagent selection and may be rendered only after a material compiler promotes a lawful PublicationOccurrence, observation, event, media program, offer or other typed owner record
  invariant a public Discover domain cut, including the default discover selection, may narrow admitted publication material only through a published SourceCollection that explicitly names both that domain and the source reference; lexical title/source matching and global-feed fallback are forbidden
  invariant protocol carriers resolve only beneath a named human action and native effect aperture; a visible Buy, Book, Reserve or Publish remains refused until the real owners close it
  invariant a Community application binding selects an explicit community through its typed material query and lowers only public canonical human body, active membership and accepted posts; it never turns federation or an external publication into speech
  invariant a Board application binding selects an explicit World through its typed material query and lowers only published WorldFragment arrangements; a Board pin may link to a published nested grammar but never impersonates the pinned subject, retained material, an offer or an action aperture
  invariant a SiteApplicationLowerer names a CUE-compiled structural operation sequence, canonical material owner and closed physical reader realization; native owner readers normalize that owner into a bounded material stream, and one generic renderer executes the opcodes without branching on application kind, source, protocol or World
  invariant a SiteApplicationLowerer also declares the one binding coordinate its canonical material reader may receive; SiteProgram lowering reads that CUE-compiled coordinate generically, so application-specific JSON field names cannot become a route-local C query ladder
  invariant SiteProgram presentation classes derive only from the CUE-compiled lowerer presentation contract and structural layout (river, state, thread, board, audio or video); the application kind remains a data coordinate, so a newly published application of an existing layout cannot require a stylesheet branch on its internal name
  invariant every field in the authored presentation-cell and lowerer inputs survives strict CUE-to-Zig parsing and generated native descriptors; an unknown semantic field fails compilation instead of becoming invisible runtime loss
  cannot_infer a SitePresentation -> studied Ghost code, donor backend, source truth, provider admission, audience entitlement or authority
  cannot_infer a SemanticSlot accepts Watch -> video material, rights to show it or a viewer identity
  cannot_infer a SourceCollection -> content, freshness, source rights, retained bodies or provider availability
  cannot_infer a CapabilityProgram -> credential, price, spend authority, payment, settlement or a completed effect
  cannot_infer an ExperienceStage -> a linear user journey, authority or a completed state transition
  cannot_infer a renderer layout -> material ownership, source admission, a provider, rights, authority or an effect
  cannot_infer WorkExample.made_with -> client account ownership, client endorsement, delivery, availability or authority to use the account's records
