architecture web-lowering
  canonical_name WebLowering
  family surface
  domain Surface / Physical realisation
  layer surface
  semantic_question Which part of this interaction does the browser already do, and what is left for script?
  purpose The public search was a JSON endpoint plus a hand-written renderer in the page that rebuilt candidate cards from it -- two ideas of what a record is, and the second pointed at addresses that answered 404, so the search failed silently and read as an empty result. The tournament is: semantic HTML and native forms first, then CSS, then a server-rendered fragment swapped by HTMX, and script only for what none of those can express. A page that renders records is a page carrying a second compiler.
  maturity implemented
  source_path cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/src/main.c
  source_path schemas/control/audience-presentation.cue
  source_path cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/tools/compile_audience_presentations.zig
  source_path cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/generated/native_audience_presentations.h
  source_path cmd/BonfyreExternalEstate/src/main.c
  source_path cmd/BonfyreExperienceMap/generated/external_bindings.jsonl
  source_path cmd/BonfyreExperienceMap/generated/stage_bindings.jsonl
  source_path cmd/BonfyreExperienceMap/generated/chains.jsonl
  source_path site/matrix/aurekai-composed.css
  source_path site/matrix/surfaces/_kit.js
  consumes SurfacePattern
  consumes CompoundingSlice
  publishes SurfaceIR
  internal_calculus one address answers both projections: declared patterns lower their own typed owner records to HTML or JSON from one query. The ExperienceMap's human chains, protocol programs, home blueprints and stage windows are compatibility/reference material only; an unmatched candidate has no stage edge, and no public donor surface may lower those references until a SiteProgram supplies typed applications, real material and native apertures. Free text is a control of every declared pattern rather than an endpoint beside one, so a surface becomes searchable by being a surface. A pattern may declare one affordance per record -- an href template whose placeholders name columns it serves -- so a row can be acted on without the page building the link.
  invariant one query, one corpus, one ordering; a human path and a machine path that read different things are two estates wearing one name
  invariant search is a capability of every pattern, not an endpoint beside one; the alternative is a second corpus for every surface that wanted to be searchable
  invariant a search ANDs with the slices rather than widening past them; narrowing to one estate and then searching must not hand back the whole table
  invariant only fields a pattern serves may appear in a record affordance, and a placeholder naming anything else drops the affordance rather than emitting a link with a hole in it
  invariant a value going into a URL is encoded for a URL; escaping it for HTML produces a link that mostly works and breaks on the first ampersand
  invariant a control that is accepted must act; limit was reserved and then ignored, so a caller asking for three rows received sixty-five and nothing said so -- which is the same silent non-narrowing the unknown-slice refusal exists to prevent, sitting inside the list of names that skip it
  invariant a limit narrows within the extent's ceiling and can never raise it; a limit that could would be a caller granting itself a density the surface was not authored at
  invariant the public page speaks no internal vocabulary; extent is this estate's word for density and a stranger has never heard it
  cannot_infer a lowered surface -> a simpler one; the work moved to the server, where it is rendered once and can be read without script
  cannot_infer a server-rendered fragment -> a cached one; it is computed per request like every other projection
  witness components/BonfyreControlPlane/tests/web-lowering.test.mjs checks that one address answers a human in HTML and a machine in JSON, that search narrows and compounds with a slice, that every pattern answers it, that the page builds no records in script, that each record carries an encoded affordance, and that the page calls no endpoint which answers 404
  invariant existing styled navigation routes receive live composition through the native SurfaceIR lowerer rather than a replacement route or browser-resident renderer
  invariant the existing public home remains its own visual compiler output while title, canonical address, territory metadata and Matrix context are emitted from the native resolved address; a styled home never becomes a host-guessed second institution
  invariant a SurfaceDemand ranks the supplied candidate reservoir by declared grammar affordances, cross-domain fit and carrier diversity; it is presentation selection, never provider admission or a replacement candidate identity
  invariant a named World demand alias is explicit and reversible; it may narrow to a declared external-world compatibility set but may not claim the addressed World is that external World
  cannot_infer an available external-estate response -> a deployed provider, admitted observation, evidence, authority, payment or effect
  witness components/BonfyreControlPlane/tests/web-lowering.test.mjs checks that one address answers a human in HTML and a machine in JSON, that search narrows and compounds with a slice, that every pattern answers it, that the page builds no records in script, that each record carries an encoded affordance, and that the page calls no endpoint which answers 404
  invariant a coarse external candidate tag is not a human product result; Discover and Stage may consume the reservoir only through a discriminating typed role and real PackDemand or WorldDemand closure
  invariant no lexical stage fallback creates an executable public edge; no compatible typed output means no edge
  invariant a public Discover, Stage, Community, Board or Listings request with HTML or wildcard representation lowers its established donor document natively; only an explicit JSON request may take a machine projection, so crawlers never receive a legacy script-owned second surface
  invariant donor templates carry numeric SurfaceProgram slots and native lowering resolves their authored CUE-compiled operations through one opcode executor; the same generated SurfaceProgram table declares root and World-route admission, so no route-specific marker dispatch, root-route ladder or legacy marker vocabulary remains executable, and browser-side data reconstruction is not a SurfaceIR program
  invariant a compiled SurfaceProgram names a portable renderer phenotype separately from its grammar key; CUE compiles the phenotype into a typed presentation record and native Web lowering dispatches only on that record's structural opcodes, never renderer-name string comparisons or visible-link-label routing
  invariant a territory's preferred subject field is an authored CUE field-selection record compiled into the same native table; the lowerer may fall back when that owned field is absent but may not use a territory-name cascade to manufacture another primary claim
  invariant generated machine carrier names and schemas are authored CUE declarations compiled into native tables; a hand-maintained route array may not decide MCP, A2A, or API carrier identity
  invariant shared home and Matrix shells request resolved identity, authored navigation, and Matrix context only through CUE-declared numeric template slots; named marker vocabulary is not a public template contract
  invariant public metadata wording for a Matrix-resolved audience is a strict CUE-to-native declaration; server code may select the resolved scope but may not retain a parallel audience-copy table
  invariant an addressed World grammar is a path cut (`/w/{published-world}/{published-grammar}`), not a frontend coordinate: it resolves only when the World owner published that exact fragment, and every resulting donor shell preserves the same World address in its next links
  invariant a Board pin is an authored World fragment, a Community entry is an accepted canonical human post, and a Listing is a published canonical offer; retained material, a draft claim, an external candidate or a carrier program may not impersonate any of them
  known_gap public Stage has no canonical published event occurrence and Listings has no canonical published offer in the current estate. Their native donor documents therefore expose their distinct empty states rather than manufacturing event or commercial activity.
  known_gap PackGraph, WorldDemand, RelationGraph and InformationPolicy joins are owed before any native public program can enrich into private or institutional closure.
  known_gap the tournament's later rungs are unbuilt: commandfor, CSS anchor positioning, declarative shadow DOM and view transitions are named in the plan and driven by nothing

interaction lowering-serves-both-projections
  source web-lowering
  destination surface-pattern
  relation projects
  preserves the record set, its order and its refusals identically in both projections; only the carrier differs
  drops nothing for the human path that the machine path receives
  forbidden_inference a rendered fragment -> an authorized action on the row it shows
  forbidden_inference an affordance on a record -> permission to perform it

architecture public-observation-aperture
  canonical_name PublicObservationAperture
  family surface
  domain Surface / Public Aperture
  layer surface/public
  semantic_question Does one public address answer a human and a machine from the same rows, or does it hand the machine the human's page?
  purpose /_surface/external-estate is the public observations aperture. It lowers one query through one reservoir and writes the answer down twice -- an HTML fragment for a reader, a records array for a client -- because a second endpoint would be a second corpus and they drift.
  maturity implemented
  node_types SurfaceFragment
  node_types MachineProjection
  edge_types lowers
  edge_types negotiates
  command BonfyreWebAddress
  command BonfyreExternalEstate
  source_path cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/src/main.c
  source_path cmd/BonfyreExternalEstate/src/main.c
  witness components/BonfyreControlPlane/tests/web-lowering.test.mjs
  invariant both projections come from one SELECT with one set of binds, one ordering and one limit; the reader chooses how the answer is written down and never which rows it is written from
  invariant a refusal answers in the reader's own media type; a machine asking for JSON is not handed an HTML refusal page
  forbidden_inference a machine projection -> an admitted provider, evidence, authority, payment, settlement or effect
  forbidden_inference serving a records array -> a stable public API; this is the same aperture, written down differently
  known_gap the aperture answered 200 text/html to `Accept: application/json`. It was never unserved -- every sibling surface (worlds, internet-census, presentation-templates) already negotiated correctly and this one route did not, so the failing surface tests were read for weeks as "nobody is running the endpoint" when the endpoint was up and handing machines a page.
  known_gap this aperture renders `article.bf-material-card` where every other surface renders `dl.surface-record`. The surface test asserts the shared pattern, so it still fails on markup after content negotiation is fixed. Restyling a live public page is a presentation decision and is left to its owner rather than taken to make a test pass.
  known_gap the fix is in the repository and the deployed host still serves the previous binary; nothing here claims the live aperture negotiates yet.

architecture clone-grammar-registry
  canonical_name CloneGrammarRegistry
  family surface
  domain Surface / Thirty product vocabularies over one set of cells
  layer contract
  semantic_question Which mature product grammars would make an organ this estate already has legible to a person, and what would actually have to be built for each?
  purpose Thirty interaction vocabularies -- a model hub, an artifact registry, an object-versioning UI, a distribution dashboard, a work tracker, a governance stack, a parent association, twenty-four others -- each declared as the interaction primitives it needs rather than as an application. Thirty-three primitives, twenty-nine bound to the architecture that already owns them and four owned by nothing and saying so. Served at /s/grammars/all, /s/grammar/<name> and /s/primitive/<name>.
  maturity measured
  node_types CloneGrammar
  node_types InteractionPrimitive
  edge_types needs
  edge_types held_by
  internal_calculus thirty applications would be thirty orphans: each re-inventing a proposal, a member, a release and a run, and none of them reaching the organs that already hold those things. A proposal from a crowdfunding pitch, a proposal in a DAO and a proposal at a parent association are one cell under three vocabularies, and built three times they can never be counted, compared or governed together
  internal_calculus a grammar is provenance in the same sense a page region records a reading rhythm: it names where an interaction vocabulary was learned, and nothing else
  internal_calculus the density claim is computed rather than asserted. How many of the thirty share a cell is counted from the declarations, so "these multiply one another" is a figure on a page instead of a sentence in a plan
  internal_calculus a cell nothing owns is the useful part of the table: it turns "this grammar is missing" into a named absence that every grammar depending on it inherits, so a surface cannot be planned over ground that does not exist
  invariant a primitive's owner must be an architecture id that exists in the atlas; a grammar naming an organ that does not exist is refused at compile time
  invariant a cell with no owner states what is missing, and a cell with an owner states no gap; the compiler refuses either contradiction
  invariant a grammar must need at least one declared cell, and a cell it names must be declared; the compiler refuses an undeclared cell and an empty grammar
  invariant the shared and unowned counts are compiled from the declaration, never written beside it, and the build refuses a page that computes them itself
  invariant a grammar waiting on an unowned cell is marked as not ready and may not claim that nothing new has to be built underneath it
  forbidden_inference a named grammar -> that its authors know this estate exists, that any of their code runs here, or that this estate reproduces their product
  forbidden_inference every cell being held -> a surface that is built; it means only that nothing new has to be invented underneath one
  forbidden_inference a cell being shared by twenty-one grammars -> twenty-one surfaces that exist, or a claim about how any of them would look
  forbidden_inference a grammar's stated wave -> a commitment to build it, a schedule, or authority to spend on it
  source_path schemas/control/clone-grammar.cue
  source_path cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/tools/compile_clone_grammars.zig
  source_path cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/generated/native_clone_grammars.h
  source_path cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/src/main.c
  source_path cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/tests/clone_grammar_test.sh
  witness 2026-09-26 thirty grammars and thirty-three primitives compiled from CUE by a generator that refuses an undeclared cell, an empty grammar, an unexplained gap and a cell claiming both an owner and a reason for having none -- all four refusals exercised in the witness
  witness 2026-09-26 every binding resolves against the live atlas: twenty-nine primitives name an owning architecture that exists among the 369, and all thirty grammars name a real organ they sit over
  witness 2026-09-26 the density is measured rather than argued. The thirty need 159 cell bindings between them and 33 cells carry all of it: member is needed by 21 of the 30, receipt by 14, schedule by 11, collection by 10, thread by 9
  witness 2026-09-26 the gap surface is four cells nothing owns -- no version control over the object estate, no outbound message rail, no bound signature, no live media path -- and nine of the thirty inherit one, so they are marked as waiting rather than presented as ready: the artifact registry, object versioning, the repository page, scheduling, community operations, live selling, publishing, the school institution and controlled documents
  witness 2026-09-26 served natively and checked against the declaration: /s/grammars/all lists all thirty and all thirty-three in two virtualised lists, /s/grammar/school-institution names seven held cells and one nothing holds and says it is not ready, and every grammar it lists as sharing really shares two or more cells -- asserted row by row rather than eyeballed
  known_gap the four unowned cells are the real work this table exposes, and none of them is built. Version, message, signature and stream are declared absences, not scheduled items
  known_gap a grammar's wave is authored judgement about ordering and carries no measurement; nothing computes what a surface would cost or yield
  known_gap the registry says which organ owns a cell and not how far that organ is from presenting it, so a grammar can rest entirely on held cells and still be a long way from a surface
  interacts grammars-name-the-organs-that-hold-them

